  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on overweighting small-probability outcomes and would favor Lottery B after adjustment. However, the individual’s reasoning emphasizes preferring the safe, certain outcome (Lottery A), showing risk-averse tendencies rather than sensitivity to rare events. The individual does not indicate any special attention to or enhancement of the low-probability outcome in Lottery B; instead, they downplay it due to its unlikelihood. There is no evidence that the individual increased the weight of the 0.1% chance or computed a transformed expected value. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is unlikely that the individual used this specific probability-weighting rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
